# Keep LF where it is load-bearing.
#
# A CRLF shell script has a broken shebang — the kernel looks for the
# interpreter "/bin/bash\r" and reports "no such file or directory", which reads
# like a missing file rather than a line-ending problem. That is exactly how the
# container ended up in a restart loop when its image was built from
# `git archive` on a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true); CI never hit it
# because GitHub runners are Linux with autocrlf=false.
#
# Normalize text in the repository, and check out / archive the executable and
# config files with LF regardless of the platform.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.vue text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# The gateway binary is copied into the image by CI; it is not text.
aisix-bin/** -text
